  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 106,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180 (Aug) and 1260 (Sep) (E-05), and this is not explained by slow response handling (median 1.6d/p90 2.8d, within 3.0d SLA; E-03) or a tariff change (0 logged changes; E-02, E-07). A measurable contributor is that manual meter-read route completion for ~9200 accounts fell to 88% vs a 95% target in Aug-Sep (E-04), which triggers estimate substitution that generates disputes: 1240 of 3025 disputed bills (41%) carry read_type ESTIMATED (E-01). The remaining 1785 disputed bills (59%, read_type ACTUAL) are not explained by estimate substitution, so the majority of the surge's cause is not yet established from committed evidence."
 },
